Directory: FISSION
File:      superheavy_gs_WMM.readme (24 May 2026)
*************************************************

                     SUPREHEAVY_GS_WMM.DAT
        Ground-state properties of isotopes with Z=98-126
  (Provided by P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, 24 May 2026)
 *****************************************************************

Contents
--------
The file contains ground-state properties calculated using the Warsaw macroscopic-microscopic (WMM) model [1].
It provides ground-state masses, total binding energies, macroscopic and microscopic energy contributions,
equilibrium deformation parameters, as well as ground-state-to-ground-state alpha-decay Q-values and nucleon
separation energies. The dataset covers 1305 heavy and superheavy nuclei with proton numbers Z=98-126 and neutron
numbers N=134-192. For a given Z, the minimum neutron number increases incrementally with Z. All calculations were
performed by minimizing the total energy with respect to seven axially symmetric deformation parameters, which
define the nuclear surface in a standard spherical-harmonic expansion. Further details of the model and computational
procedure can be found in Ref. [1].

Format
------
Each record of the file contains

     Z      : proton (charge) number
     N      : neutron number
     A      : mass number
     M      : ground-state mass excess [MeV]
     Etot   : total ground-state energy [MeV]
     Emac   : macroscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     Emic   : microscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     b2-b8  : equilibrium deformation parameters
     Qa     : ground-state-to-ground-state alpha-decay Q-value [MeV]
     Sp     : one-proton separation energy [MeV]
     Sn     : one-neutron separation energy [MeV]
     S2p    : two-proton separation energy [MeV]
     S2n    : two-neutron separation energy [MeV]

The corresponding Fortran format specification is (3i4,16f8.2).

References
----------
[1] P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 138, 101393 (2021).
